59b914b5-0798-48c3-99e7-18a9942e195c	note	Vehicle research — use case and requirements.\n\nCurrent vehicle: Volvo S60 hybrid (sedan). Looking to move to an SUV or crossover for easier ingress/egress and more comfort. Likes how the S60 drives but prefers BMW's driving feel overall.\n\nOpen to electric — daily 30-40mi round trip makes it very practical.\n\nLong trips: Boston, MA to past Wilmington, DE (~400mi). Done a few times a year. Currently a single 6-8h drive, but timing is tight trying to thread Boston and Wilmington rush hours. Actively leaning toward splitting into 2 days (~200mi/day, 3-4h driving each). At 200mi/day, range anxiety is essentially zero for any of the candidates.\n\nCharging at destination: Limited — only Tesla Superchargers at gas stations at either end of Wilmington. One of the candidate cars touted native Tesla charging support, but all of them can use Tesla Superchargers with an NACS adapter, so this isn't a real differentiator.\n\nKey requirements:\n- SUV or crossover body style (easier to get in/out vs. sedan)\n- Comfort priority\n- ~400mi range preferred, but 200mi+ is sufficient given the trip-splitting plan\n- Electric preferred (current hybrid barely uses gas except on long trips)\n- Integrated dash cam would be a nice-to-have (seen in newer Audis)\n\nDecision outlook: Comes down to the iX3 interior. If it feels like a proper BMW (not like the i3), it's likely the pick. EX60 is the solid fallback given familiarity with Volvo. Both arrive summer 2026 — test drives will be the deciding factor.	"{\\"topics\\": [\\"vehicle-research\\", \\"vehicle-features\\"], \\"classification_confidence\\": 0.95}"	[-0.011125846,-0.01714964,0.008380086,0.0015773516,-0.022005027,-0.0008965913,0.001608996,0.024406757,0.06693683,0.045516003,-0.017668935,-0.067300335,-0.05250049,0.0028431274,0.025315518,0.032300007,0.016435614,-0.029625649,-0.0229787,0.012794074,0.030300729,0.027133042,0.03564944,-0.012820038,-0.0074972883,-0.048060536,-0.0387652,0.019642245