fb1c24d9-ef5e-432b-a42d-5206ea05a696	note	# NTL-Torrent Project\n\n**Location:** C:\\Users\\nazuraki\\Documents\\ntl-torrent\n**Repo:** Not a git repo (as of 2026-03-11)\n\n## What it is\nElectron desktop torrent client. Go backend handles downloading (anacrolix/torrent + SQLite), Svelte frontend is the UI, Electron glues them together.\n\n## Stack\n- **Backend:** Go 1.22, module `github.com/ntl/ntl-torrent`, chi router, gorilla/websocket, modernc.org/sqlite (pure-Go, no CGO), anacrolix/torrent\n- **Frontend:** Svelte 4, Vite 5\n- **Electron:** v29, electron-store for persistence\n- **DB:** SQLite WAL mode, MaxOpenConns=1\n\n## Layout\n```\nntl-torrent/\n  backend/\n    go.mod\n    cmd/ntl-backend/main.go\n    internal/api/server.go middleware.go handlers.go hub.go\n    internal/config/config.go\n    internal/db/db.go migrate.go\n    internal/torrent/engine.go id.go\n  frontend/\n    package.json vite.config.js\n    src/main.js App.svelte lib/nodes.js lib/TorrentRow.svelte lib/TorrentDetail.svelte ...\n  electron/\n    package.json\n    src/main.js src/preload.js\n  package.json   ← monorepo root (npm workspaces)\n  CLAUDE.md CONTEXT.md\n```\n\n## Key commands\n- Build backend: `cd backend && go build -o ../electron/resources/ntl-backend.exe ./cmd/ntl-backend`\n- Dev: `npm run dev` (root) — Vite on 5173 + Electron\n- Go binary: `C:\\Program Files\\Go\\bin\\go.exe`\n\n## Architecture notes\n- Backend prints `LISTENING:<port>` to stdout; Electron reads it to discover port\n- Frontend calls backend via REST + WebSocket; multi-node support (node_id on every torrent)\n- Auth: empty APIKey = local trusted mode; X-API-Key header for remote nodes\n- Watch folders scan for .torrent files every 5s; progress emitted over WS every 1s\n- Pause = CancelPieces; Resume = DownloadAll; file skip = PiecePriorityNone\n\n## DB tables\n- watch_folders, torrents, torrent_files, remote_nodes, settings\n\n## Status\n- REST API fully implemented (torrents, watch-folders, remote-nodes CRUD)\n