d79d689a-e5f2-45ef-9701-74a67640581b	note	# WoW AddOn Suite\n\n**Location:** `C:\\Program Files (x86)\\World of Warcraft\\_retail_\\Interface\\AddOns`\n**Repo:** Git repo, branch: `main`\n\n## What it is\nWoW Retail addon suite by Nazuraki. No build step, no package manager. Testing in-game via `/reload` and `/nui test [key]`. Interface 120000+.\n\n## Addons\n\n| Addon | Purpose | Commands |\n|---|---|---|\n| **LibNAddOn** | Bootstrapping factory; all addons depend on this | `/lib` |\n| **LibNUI** | OOP UI widget library; global `LibNUI` | `/nui test [key]` |\n| **LibNUI_Test** | Visual test harness (LoadOnDemand) | — |\n| **Warbandeer_Characters** | Data layer; populates `WarbandeerApi` global | — |\n| **Warbandeer** | Main character viewer UI | `/warband`, `/wb` |\n| **Warbandeer_Alias** | Guild chat alias prefix | — |\n| **Warbandeer_Collected** | Transmog tracker | `/collected`, `/collect` |\n| **ShadowsOfUI-XP** | Minimal full-width XP bar; hides Blizzard's bar; below max level only | — |\n| **HideStanceBar** | Hides stance bar | — |\n| **HideBagBar** | Hides bag bar (raw WoW API, no LibN) | — |\n| **CombatOutline** | Combat outline UI (LibNAddOn only, no LibNUI) | — |\n| **Recycle** | (LibNUI dependent) | — |\n\n## Dependency Graph\n```\nLibNAddOn\n    +-- LibNUI → LibNUI_Test (LoadOnDemand)\n          +-- ShadowsOfUI-XP\n          +-- HideStanceBar\n          +-- Warbandeer_Alias\n          +-- Recycle\n          +-- Warbandeer_Characters (populates WarbandeerApi)\n                +-- Warbandeer\n                +-- Warbandeer_Collected\n    +-- CombatOutline (no LibNUI)\nHideBagBar (no LibN at all)\n```\n\n## Coding Conventions\n- Namespace: `local _, ns = ...` in every file\n- Class: `local Foo = Class(Parent, function(self) ... end, { defaults })`\n- Addon init: `LibNAddOn{ name=..., addOn=ns, ... }` (table) or `local ns = LibNAddOn(...)` (assignment)\n- DB migration: `MigrateDB()` auto-called on version mismatch\n- Events: `ns:registerEvent("EVENT", handler)` or `function ns.EVENT_NAME(self, ...) end`\n- Widget access: always `self._widget`; never from outside a class\n- Shared API data: `ns.api.*` (bound from `X-NUI-API` toc field)\n- LuaLS annotations on all classes/public methods\n\n## Naming\n- Public methods: `PascalCase`\n- Lifecycle hooks/callbacks: `camelCase` (onLoad, onUpdate)\n- Constructor init fields: `camelCase` (cellWidth, headerHeight)\n- Internal fields: `_prefixed` (_widget, _tabs)\n\n## Key Gotchas\n- **TableFrame offsetX/offsetY**: computed once at construction; pass `rowNames = {}` / `colNames = {}` for dynamic tables\n- **SecureButton**: never call `SetAttribute` during combat (taint)\n- **`special = true`**: registers frame in `_G` and `UISpecialFrames` (Escape closes it); top-level windows only\n- **Frame `onUpdate` elapsed**: arrives in milliseconds (Frame multiplies WoW's seconds by 1000)\n- **`ns.delay(ms, fn)`**: only one active timer per addon — new call overwrites pending\n- **`rgba(r, g, b, a)`**: r/g/b are 0–255 integers, a is 0–1 float\n\n## Getter/Setter Pattern\n```lua\nfunction MyClass:Value(v)\n    if v == nil then return self._widget:GetValue() end\n    self._widget:SetValue(v)\n    return self\nend\n```	"{\\"tags\\": [\\"wow\\", \\"lua\\", \\"addon\\", \\"warbandeer\\", \\"libnui\\", \\"project-reference\\"], \\"status\\": \\"active\\", \\"topics\\": [\\"software-development\\", \\"world-of-warcraft\\", \\"lua\\", \\"addon-development\\", \\"game-modding\\"], \\"classification_confidence\\": 0.95}"	[-0.042388916,0.02406311,0.025360107,0.006538391,0.016159058,-0.0046577454,-0.04159546,-0.051971436,-0.028427124,-0.019363403,-0.004966736,1.847744e-05,0.0026073456,0.013595581,0.01940918,0.054840088,-0.028640747,0.018096924,-0.0009703636,0.04043579,0.045013428,-0.014030457,0.011795044,0.032958984,-0.01939392,-0.03527832,-0.023025513,0.03326416,0.0024318695,-0.01260376,0.0657959,-0.028656006,0.023880005,0.05392456,-0.040008545,0.0057144165,0.057434082,-0.013648987,0.008171082,-0.0275